    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass \u2014 the full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA structured address form alongside the backward-compatible flat `address`.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string properties to `OwnerFields` (so they appear on both the request DTO and the `Owner` response DTO).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list \u2014 the \"either form\" rule can't be expressed as a per-field `@NotNull`, so validity is now enforced in the pipeline. This only loosens the contract, so earlier minimal owners still validate.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `Owner` entity: added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields, columns and accessors.\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four dialect schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`); tests run on `hsqldb`.\n- MapStruct maps the new fields by name automatically \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n\n**Create path (`ValidateOwnerFields`)**\n- New `applyAddress` step: normalizes whichever address fields are supplied, prefers structured (non-blank `addressLine1`) over the flat `address`, and sets `address` to the composed value \u2014 normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` when present. An owner with neither form is a required-field 400.\n- Fixed a latent NPE: `Localities.region(null)` blew up (500) when a postcode was present but city missing; postcode range validation now short-circuits on a blank city so the missing city correctly returns 400.\n\n**Update path (`ApplyOwner`)**\n- Mirrored the prefer-structured / compose logic so PUT stays consistent with the new fields.\n\nEverything that reads the address (household hash, postcode validation, locality) reads `postcode`/`city` \u2014 structured fields that are identical across both forms \u2014 and the composed value is stored in `Owner.address`, so all address readers see the structured value when present. Tests Cp01/Cp12/Cp29/Cp30/Cp36/Cp44 (and the other 49) are green.",
